@startuml InquiryScope

title Inquiry Scope API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox

actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Inquiry Scope Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "t_user_access_token" as t_user_access_token
    database "m_scope" as m_scope
end box

user -> page: Read scopes with optional filters and pagination
activate page
    page -> api: GET v1/author/scope (Bearer JWT, UTC timestamp; query only)
    activate api
        api -> app: [**InquiryScopeQueryHandler**] Process request
        activate app
            note over app, infra
                Execution order: validate query/header/body and checked pagination (400) -> verify JWT/roles (401) -> begin
                read-only repeatable-read transaction -> fresh now/expiry -> joined current credential/user (401) -> claims
                permission (403) -> count -> optional page -> complete mapping -> COMMIT -> 200. Every post-BEGIN rejection
                rolls back.
            end note
            app -> app: Generate requestId; validate UTC timestamp, known single query keys/no body, UUID id, positive signed Int64 pages/default 1/10/pageSize <=100 and ACTIVE/INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED filter
            note over app, infra
                Reject unknown/repeated keys and malformed header/query with 400 E10001 before SQL. Generate requestId if
                omitted. Supplied id is a non-empty UUID, never null; omitted id is typed SQL NULL. pageIndex/pageSize are
                positive signed 64-bit integers, default 1/10 only when omitted, pageSize at most 100. Compute checked
                offset = (pageIndex - 1) * pageSize and reject parse/offset overflow beyond nonnegative BIGINT with 400.
                Explicit empty/null-like values do not become defaults. Row status must be one of ACTIVE, INACTIVE, LOCKED,
                ARCHIVED.
            end note
            app -> app: Compute checked offset = (pageIndex - 1) * pageSize; reject numeric/offset overflow beyond nonnegative BIGINT
            alt Invalid input or pagination overflow
                break Reject this inquiry
                    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
                    api -> page: Show failure without a partial scope page
                    page -> user: Display failure; no scope data
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and structured unique roleIds/name array
            alt Missing/invalid JWT or malformed roles
                break Reject this inquiry
                    app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                    api -> page: Show failure without a partial scope page
                    page -> user: Display failure; no scope data
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: callerUserId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT
            app -> app: Bind omitted id/searchPattern/rowStatus as typed SQL NULL; supplied searchPattern = percent + search + percent, preserving ILIKE wildcards
            app -> infra: BEGIN REPEATABLE READ READ ONLY
            note over app, infra
                Verify Bearer JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and structured roles before BEGIN. roles must be
                an array including [], every role object has UUID roleId and non-empty string name, and roleIds are unique.
                Missing/malformed roles is generic 401 E10002, never an empty-list or live-grant fallback. Derive
                callerUserId only from verified sub and accessTokenHash as SHA-256 of the exact JWT; do not accept caller
                ids or isPlatformAdmin flags from requests.
                Require matching token hash/caller id, ACTIVE token/user and strict expired_at > now;
                missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched credentials is generic 401 E10002 with rollback before scope
                reads. No user/role/token locks or writes. This current credential gate preserves immediate logout/reset
                revocation (Q13).
            end note
            activate infra
            alt Read and mapping work completes
                note over app, infra
                    No locks or writes. Credentials, scope count and page use one repeatable-read snapshot.
                    Timeout or unexpected SQL/result/mapping failure may interrupt any step; no partial response.
                end note
                app -> app: Capture fresh server UTC now immediately before joined credential read; recheck JWT exp
                alt JWT expired before fresh credential read
                    break Reject this inquiry
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Show failure without a partial scope page
                        page -> user: Display failure; no scope data
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                infra -> t_user_access_token: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                activate t_user_access_token
                    note right of t_user_access_token
                        SELECT
                            at.id as access_token_id
                        FROM authen.t_user_access_token at
                        JOIN authen.m_user u ON u.id = at.user_id
                        WHERE at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                        AND at.user_id = '<sequence.callerUserId>'
                        AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    end note
                    t_user_access_token -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                deactivate t_user_access_token
                infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                alt Current token/user missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched
                    break Reject this inquiry
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Show failure without a partial scope page
                        page -> user: Display failure; no scope data
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Authorize once using exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT roles; never reload current grants
                alt No exact PLATFORM_ADMIN role claim
                    break Reject this inquiry
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 403 E10009 You do not have permission to read scopes.
                        api -> page: Show failure without a partial scope page
                        page -> user: Display failure; no scope data
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Get total items
                infra -> m_scope: QUERY - Get total items
                activate m_scope
                    note right of m_scope
                        SELECT
                            COUNT(s.id) as total_items
                        FROM author.m_scope s
                        WHERE s.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                        AND ('<sequence.id>' IS NULL OR s.id = '<sequence.id>') -- only when id is specified
                        AND ('<sequence.searchPattern>' IS NULL OR s.scope ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>' OR s.description ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>') -- only when search is specified
                        AND ('<sequence.rowStatus>' IS NULL OR s.row_status = '<sequence.rowStatus>') -- only when rowStatus is specified
                    end note
                    m_scope -> infra: Return totalItems for non-DELETED scopes and all nullable filters
                deactivate m_scope
                infra -> app: Return totalItems for non-DELETED scopes and all nullable filters
                app -> app: totalPages = 0 when totalItems=0, otherwise integer quotient plus nonzero remainder; no floating point or overflowing count+pageSize-1
                alt totalItems = 0
                    app -> app: items = []; skip page query; totalPages = 0
                else totalItems > 0
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Get scopes
                    infra -> m_scope: QUERY - Get scopes
                    activate m_scope
                        note right of m_scope
                            SELECT
                                s.id as scope_id,
                                s.scope,
                                s.name,
                                s.description,
                                s.row_status
                            FROM author.m_scope s
                            WHERE s.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                            AND ('<sequence.id>' IS NULL OR s.id = '<sequence.id>') -- only when id is specified
                            AND ('<sequence.searchPattern>' IS NULL OR s.scope ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>' OR s.description ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>') -- only when search is specified
                            AND ('<sequence.rowStatus>' IS NULL OR s.row_status = '<sequence.rowStatus>') -- only when rowStatus is specified
                            ORDER BY s.scope, s.id
                            LIMIT '<sequence.pageSize>' OFFSET '<sequence.offset>'
                        end note
                        m_scope -> infra: Return five-field scope rows in scope/id order from identical filters/snapshot
                    deactivate m_scope
                    infra -> app: Return five-field scope rows in scope/id order from identical filters/snapshot
                    app -> app: Require page row count = min(pageSize, max(0, totalItems-offset)); mismatch is internal failure
                    alt Page contains rows
                        app -> app: Map exactly scopeId/scope/name/description/rowStatus per row; required values non-null; exclude caller/assignment/token/hash/audit
                    else Page beyond range contains no rows
                        app -> app: items = []; retain positive totalItems/totalPages; no 404
                    end
                end
                app -> app: data = exactly items/pageIndex/pageSize/totalItems/totalPages; echo validated page values; explicit empty arrays; finish full mapping
                app -> infra: COMMIT
                infra -> app: Return committed consistent read-only scope page
                note over app, infra
                    Approved by the product owner (answered through the lead SA, 2026-11-06; claims basis A12); use exact
                    PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT role claims under [owner-confirmed
                    review](../../../../../docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-07-api-review-design.md), Q2/Q4/Q10/Q13. This detailed
                    revision remains in-review; no backend/schema implementation.
                    Omitted searchPattern binds typed SQL NULL; supplied search, including empty string, becomes one bound text
                    searchPattern = percent + search + percent, preserving percent/underscore wildcards. Never interpolate
                    client text into SQL. The three nullable filters disable only themselves and combine by AND; id is still
                    filtered/paginated, not an unpaged alternate path.
                    After current credentials pass, authorize once using exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT
                    roles. Valid roles=[] or any other role name is 403 E10009 `You do not have permission to read scopes.`
                    after rollback and before count/page SQL. Never query current caller role assignments to grant, remove or
                    replace authorization. Grant withdrawal after token issuance leaves the old privilege usable until access
                    expiry (Q4); refresh reloads current grants (Q7). Scope metadata returned below comes from the database
                    snapshot, distinct from author/me's calling-token snapshot.
                    Count first and optionally fetch the page in the same read-only repeatable-read snapshot as credentials.
                    Both scope queries use identical non-DELETED/id/searchPattern/rowStatus WHERE predicates; every supplied
                    value is bound, including pageSize and checked offset. If totalItems=0 skip the page SQL and return
                    items=[], totalPages=0. With positive count, query the requested page; an offset beyond the range returns
                    items=[] with positive totals/pages and no 404. A missing/DELETED id is the same empty-list 200 for an
                    authorized caller; permission is checked before revealing whether any scope exists.
                    Scopes with rowStatus DELETED are never returned. Omitted rowStatus preserves every non-DELETED status;
                    supplied status accepts only ACTIVE/INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED. Sort by scope then id ascending, preserving
                    database collation. This is deterministic within one snapshot; later requests may see newly committed
                    changes and are not a frozen paging cursor.
                    Map each row to exactly scopeId/scope/name/description/rowStatus. No caller id, assignment, token/hash,
                    audit or extra table fields are returned. Return exactly five data keys:
                    items/pageIndex/pageSize/totalItems/totalPages, with explicit empty arrays. Echo validated pages and compute
                    totalPages by integer quotient/remainder (zero when count=0), avoiding floating point or overflowing
                    count+pageSize-1. Require page row count = min(pageSize, max(0, totalItems-offset)); mismatch or
                    malformed/null/missing required data is internal failure.
                    Map the full response before COMMIT, then HTTP 200 S10000 Inquiry Scope Success. An unexpected
                    SQL/result/mapping error rolls back and returns generic 500 without bizCode; timeout before COMMIT rolls
                    back and returns 408 E90001. Never return partially mapped rows, mutate scopes/assignments/tokens/audit, or
                    answer 404/409 for this inquiry.
                end note
                app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Inquiry Scope Success; all five pagination keys
                api -> page: Show authorized scope page and totals
                page -> user: Display scopes or empty page
            else Timeout before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
                api -> page: Show failure without a partial scope page
                page -> user: Display failure; no scope data
            else Unexpected SQL/result/mapping failure before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
                api -> page: Show failure without a partial scope page
                page -> user: Display failure; no scope data
            end
            deactivate infra
        deactivate app
    deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
